From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: nss: use ethernet frame mode with NSS offload

With nss_offload=1 and frame_mode=1 (native Wi-Fi), clients associate
but never finish WPA: the 4-way handshake times out (reason 15) on both
radios of IPQ5018 + QCN6122. The AP transmits its EAPOL messages, but the
clients' replies never reach the host. NSS's per-peer stats count nothing
received from them, not even as unauthorized-peer drops, so they are lost
below NSS. The same setup with frame_mode=2 works, and frame_mode=2 is
what the donor pairs with nss_offload=1.

Rather than bring up an AP no client can join, warn at probe and use
ethernet mode when NSS offload is on. Mesh vdevs use native Wi-Fi on
their own and are unaffected. Raw mode was never tried with NSS and is
overridden the same way. Issue #24.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2956,6 +2956,18 @@
 	}
 	ab->nss.enabled = nss_offload;
 
+	/* With NSS offload, AP and station vdevs are only known to work in
+	 * Ethernet mode. In native Wi-Fi mode the clients' EAPOL frames never
+	 * reach the host, so no client gets past the 4-way handshake; raw mode
+	 * was never tried with NSS. Mesh vdevs use native Wi-Fi on their own
+	 * and are not affected by frame_mode.
+	 */
+	if (nss_offload && ath11k_frame_mode != ATH11K_HW_TXRX_ETHERNET) {
+		ath11k_warn(ab, "frame_mode %u does not work with nss_offload, using ethernet (2)\n",
+			    ath11k_frame_mode);
+		ath11k_frame_mode = ATH11K_HW_TXRX_ETHERNET;
+	}
+
 	if (nss_offload)
 		ab->nss.stats_enabled = 1;
 
